source binding/reference frozenset in _in_scope_dirs@72; its value/role follows this source operation, not a universal meaning shared with other scopes: def _in_scope_dirs(scope: frozenset[str]) -> frozenset[str]:
    """Every ancestor directory (repo-relative posix) of an in-scope file."""
    # ls shows only dirs holding in-scope files: an excluded file's NAME must not leak
    dirs: set[str] = set()
    for rel in scope:
        parts = rel.split("/")[:-1]
        for depth in range(1, len(parts) + 1):
            dirs.add("/".join(parts[:depth]))
    return frozenset(dirs)

