source binding/reference str in _elide_data_uris@111; its value/role follows this source operation, not a universal meaning shared with other scopes: def _elide_data_uris(text: str) -> str:
    # Neutralise the MARKER, not just the payload: never restore it; replacement has no \n
    text = _DATA_URI_RX.sub(
        lambda m: (f"[data-uri {m.group(1)} elided: {len(m.group(2))} chars]"
                   if m.group(2) else f"[data-uri {m.group(1)} elided]"),
        text)
    return _DATA_URI_IMAGE_RX.sub(
        lambda m: (f"[data-uri image/{m.group(1)} elided]"
                   if m.group(1) else "[data-uri image elided]"),
        text)

source binding/reference bool in _excluded_target@75; its value/role follows this source operation, not a universal meaning shared with other scopes: def _excluded_target(rel: str, scope: frozenset[str] | None) -> bool:
    """_excluded_rel for an explicit Grep target, which unlike a Read target may name a directory."""
    if _always_allowed(rel):
        return False
    parts = rel.split("/")
    if any(part.lower() in _ALWAYS_EXCLUDED_DIRS for part in parts):
        return True
    if scope is None or rel in scope:
        return False
    prefix = rel + "/"
    return not any(f.startswith(prefix) for f in scope)

