source binding/reference int in _cap_int@39; its value/role follows this source operation, not a universal meaning shared with other scopes: def _cap_int(s2: object, key: str, default: int) -> int:
    """An operator-configured integer cap; 0 survives, anything unusable falls back to `default`."""
    v = getattr(s2, key, None)
    if v is None:
        return default
    try:
        n = int(v)
    except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError):
        return default
    return n if n >= 0 else default

