source binding/reference Threat in _covered_boundaries@243; its value/role follows this source operation, not a universal meaning shared with other scopes: def _covered_boundaries(threats: list[Threat], pool: set[int],
                        boundaries: list[TrustBoundary]) -> set[str]:
    """Entry-point names covered by a threat at one of the positions in `pool`."""
    # Positions, not ids: models reuse one id across threats, which an id-keyed pool collapses
    covered: set[str] = set()
    for b in boundaries:
        bnorm = b.entry_point.strip().casefold()
        for i in pool:
            if threats[i].surface.strip().casefold() == bnorm:
                covered.add(b.entry_point)

