source binding/reference ThreatModel in _warn_output_caps@81; its value/role follows this source operation, not a universal meaning shared with other scopes: def _warn_output_caps(raw: tuple[int, int, int], tm: ThreatModel,
                      limits: tuple[int, int, int]) -> None:
    """Warn for each step2 output cap that dropped part of the threat model, naming its key."""
    kept = (len(tm.threats), len(tm.assets), len(tm.trust_boundaries))
    for (kind, key, counter), total, n, limit in zip(_OUTPUT_CAPS, raw, kept, limits):
        if n >= total:
            continue
        if counter:
            COUNTERS.bump(counter, total - n)
        log.warning(Event.S2_CAP_TRUNCATED, kind=ki

